  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find the value of $|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -4\\end{aligned}|.$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -4\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(4-0)-0+0 \\\\  & =1\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
